<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Islay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Islay is the southernmost island of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-hebrides">Inner Hebrides</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the home of the Cenél nÓengusa of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, and from the 14th century it was the heart of the Lordship of the Isles, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finlaggan">Finlaggan</a>. It is now known for its farming, its birdlife and its whisky distilleries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/islay.jpg" alt="Islay" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J M Briscoe · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_Ellen,_Islay.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
